            <ArticleTitle>Interscan variability of coronary artery calcium quantification using an electrocardiographically pulsed spiral computed tomographic protocol.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1153-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The use of an electrocardiographically pulsed spiral computed tomographic protocol significantly reduced the radiation dose to patients who underwent coronary calcium screening. For Agatston scores &lt;10, the interscan variability of such a protocol was significantly lower than that for a sequential acquisition protocol. At higher Agatston scores, the 2 protocols had similar variability characteristics.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
